sequenceDiagram
    actor Admin
    participant AdminUI as Admin UI
    participant AdminAPI as Admin API
    participant CreateKeyWF as createApiKeysWorkflow
    participant ApiKeyService as IApiKeyModuleService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant AuthMiddleware as Admin Auth Middleware
    participant StoreMiddleware as Store Channel Middleware

    Note over Admin, DB: Scenario 1: Create Secret API Key
    Admin->>AdminUI: Create new API key\n(title: "CI/CD Pipeline Key", type: secret)
    AdminUI->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/api-keys\n{ title, type: "secret" }
    AdminAPI->>CreateKeyWF: run({ title, type, created_by })

    CreateKeyWF->>CreateKeyWF: generate random token\n"sk_live_abc123...xyz789"
    CreateKeyWF->>CreateKeyWF: bcrypt.genSalt()
    CreateKeyWF->>CreateKeyWF: bcrypt.hash(token, salt) → hash
    CreateKeyWF->>CreateKeyWF: compute redacted = "sk_...z789"

    CreateKeyWF->>ApiKeyService: createApiKeys([{ token: hash, salt, redacted, title, type, created_by }])
    ApiKeyService->>DB: INSERT api_key (hash stored in token field)
    DB-->>ApiKeyService: ApiKey record (no plaintext token)
    ApiKeyService-->>CreateKeyWF: ApiKeyDTO

    CreateKeyWF-->>AdminAPI: { ...ApiKeyDTO, token: "sk_live_abc123...xyz789" }
    AdminAPI-->>AdminUI: 201 Created { api_key: { ..., token: "sk_live_..." } }
    AdminUI-->>Admin: ⚠️ Copy this token now — it won't be shown again!

    Note over Admin, DB: Scenario 2: Secret Key Authentication (CI/CD Request)
    Admin->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/products\nAuthorization: Bearer sk_live_abc123...xyz789
    AdminAPI->>AuthMiddleware: validate bearer token
    AuthMiddleware->>ApiKeyService: authenticate("sk_live_abc123...xyz789")
    ApiKeyService->>DB: SELECT api_key WHERE type='secret' AND revoked_at IS NULL
    DB-->>ApiKeyService: active secret keys
    ApiKeyService->>ApiKeyService: bcrypt.compare(inputToken, storedHash) → match found
    ApiKeyService->>DB: UPDATE api_key SET last_used_at = NOW() WHERE id = 'apk_01'
    ApiKeyService-->>AuthMiddleware: ApiKeyDTO (authenticated)
    AuthMiddleware-->>AdminAPI: request authorized
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 200 OK { products }

    Note over Admin, DB: Scenario 3: Key Rotation
    Admin->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/api-keys { title: "CI/CD Key v2", type: "secret" }
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 201 Created { token: "sk_live_new..." }
    Note over Admin: Deploy new token to CI/CD
    Admin->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/api-keys/:old_id/revoke
    AdminAPI->>ApiKeyService: revokeApiKeys(["apk_old"])
    ApiKeyService->>DB: UPDATE api_key\nSET revoked_at = NOW(), revoked_by = 'user_01'\nWHERE id = 'apk_old'
    DB-->>ApiKeyService: OK
    ApiKeyService-->>AdminAPI: ApiKeyDTO { revoked_at: "2025-06-20T..." }
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 200 OK — old key revoked immediately

    Note over Admin, DB: Scenario 4: Publishable Key — Storefront Channel Scoping
    Admin->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/api-keys { title: "EU Storefront", type: "publishable" }
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 201 Created { token: "pk_live_eu123..." }
    Admin->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/api-keys/:id/sales-channels/batch\n{ add: ["sc_eu", "sc_de"] }
    ApiKeyService->>DB: INSERT module_link (api_key_id, sales_channel_id) for each channel
    DB-->>ApiKeyService: OK
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 200 OK — channels linked

    Note over Admin, StoreMiddleware: Store API request with publishable key
    Admin->>AdminAPI: GET /store/products\nx-publishable-api-key: pk_live_eu123...
    AdminAPI->>StoreMiddleware: resolve sales channels
    StoreMiddleware->>ApiKeyService: listApiKeys({ token: "pk_live_eu123..." })
    ApiKeyService->>DB: SELECT api_key WHERE token = 'pk_live_eu123...' AND revoked_at IS NULL
    DB-->>ApiKeyService: ApiKeyDTO (publishable)
    StoreMiddleware->>DB: SELECT linked sales_channels via module link
    DB-->>StoreMiddleware: [sc_eu, sc_de]
    StoreMiddleware-->>AdminAPI: context scoped to [sc_eu, sc_de]
    AdminAPI-->>Admin: 200 OK { products } (filtered by EU sales channels)
